00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.031
By the end you will be able to:

107
00:06:40.311 --> 00:06:46.562
Design the multi-stage pipeline: retrieval, feature fetch, ranking, re-ranking and business rules.

108
00:06:46.842 --> 00:06:51.258
Choose and blend candidate sources and measure retrieval recall (L1).

109
00:06:51.538 --> 00:06:55.229
Train rankers from logs without learning their own bias (L2).

110
00:06:55.509 --> 00:07:01.375
Serve within a latency budget: feature stores, batching, caching, precomputation (L3).

111
00:07:01.655 --> 00:07:07.053
Keep the loop healthy: exploration, cold start, diversity and guardrails (L4).

112
00:07:08.403 --> 00:07:09.277
Part 2.

113
00:07:09.557 --> 00:07:11.435
Core Concepts, Beginner to Deep.

114
00:07:12.685 --> 00:07:15.330
Intuition: the shop assistant with a notebook.

115
00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:26.597
A good assistant remembers what you usually buy (buy again), knows what goes with it (bread, then butter), knows what's popular, and occasionally suggests something new to see if you'll like it.

116
00:07:26.877 --> 00:07:29.522
They also know what's actually on the shelf today.

117
00:07:29.802 --> 00:07:37.183
A recommendation system is that assistant, working for millions of customers at once, and learning from how they respond.

118
00:07:38.533 --> 00:07:39.493
Requirements.

119
00:07:39.773 --> 00:07:40.627
Functional.

120
00:07:40.907 --> 00:07:46.475
Assemble a personalised home screen: several carousels, each with 10 to 20 products.

121
00:07:46.755 --> 00:07:51.256
Only show items available at the customer's dark store, with correct prices.

122
00:07:51.536 --> 00:08:00.048
Respect business rules: pinned banners, promotions, excluded categories (for example, no alcohol where not permitted), frequency caps.

123
00:08:00.328 --> 00:08:03.656
Learn from impressions, clicks, add-to-cart and purchases.

124
00:08:03.936 --> 00:08:05.045
Non-functional.

125
00:08:06.395 --> 00:08:14.267
p99 150 ms server-side at ~400 req per second peak (with bursts during campaigns).

126
00:08:14.547 --> 00:08:19.475
Freshness: stock within seconds; purchase history within minutes; models daily.

127
00:08:19.755 --> 00:08:25.153
Degrade gracefully: if ranking fails, fall back to a cached or non-personalised feed.

128
00:08:26.503 --> 00:08:28.081
The multi-stage pipeline.

129
00:08:28.361 --> 00:08:48.244
On screen: retrieve (~400 candidates from several sources, cheap). then filter (availability, eligibility, already in cart). then fetch features (item, user, user times item, context). then rank (learned model, ~40 per carousel). then re-rank (diversity, business rules, exploration slots,

130
00:08:48.524 --> 00:08:54.092
dedupe across carousels). then render (carousels, tracking ids for every impression).

131
00:08:56.942 --> 00:09:02.467
Each stage narrows the set so the next, more expensive stage can afford to look more carefully.

132
00:09:02.747 --> 00:09:07.867
Retrieval must have high recall; ranking decides order; re-ranking applies policy.

133
