168
00:10:24.752 --> 00:10:34.949
Item-to-item (co-purchase, normalised by popularity so everything isn't goes with milk) finds complements and genuine discovery, personal to the basket.

169
00:10:35.229 --> 00:10:39.475
Best-sellers handle cold starts and trends, but they're the same for everyone.

170
00:10:40.825 --> 00:10:55.395
Other sources at scale: embedding retrieval (two-tower models: user and item vectors, approximate nearest neighbour search, Ch 22 L4 built HNSW), category affinity, seasonal and promotional lists.

171
00:10:55.675 --> 00:11:03.057
Quotas between sources are a product decision: the blend traded ~6 points of recall for thousands of discoveries.

172
00:11:03.337 --> 00:11:04.339
Measure both.

173
00:11:05.689 --> 00:11:07.844
Ranking and the bias in your own logs.

174
00:11:08.124 --> 00:11:20.775
The ranker predicts the probability of engagement (click, add-to-cart, purchase) per candidate from features, historically logistic regression and gradient-boosted trees, now also deep models.

175
00:11:21.055 --> 00:11:25.300
Its training data is the impression log, which the previous ranker produced.

176
00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:34.028
L2 made the bias visible: clicks = P(examined position) times relevance, and the old ranker put popular items on top.

