204
00:12:40.563 --> 00:12:50.653
Position bias: users look at the top more; treat position as a feature during training and fix it at serving, or weight examples by 1 or P(examined).

205
00:12:50.933 --> 00:12:54.219
Selection bias: items never shown have no labels.

206
00:12:54.499 --> 00:12:57.123
Only exploration (L4) fixes that.

207
00:12:57.403 --> 00:12:59.792
Label choice: clicks reward clickbait.

208
00:13:00.072 --> 00:13:08.968
For grocery, add-to-cart and purchase are better targets; combine them in a multi-objective score with guardrails (margin, availability).

209
00:13:09.248 --> 00:13:17.675
Offline, then online: offline metrics on logged data are biased by the same loop; confirm with A or B tests or interleaving.

