00:25:14.001 --> 00:25:20.721
Point-in-time training sets from the lake; online Redis with per-user hashes; stock via inventory events.

418
00:25:21.001 --> 00:25:23.775
Exploration (ADR-293).

419
00:25:24.055 --> 00:25:29.153
Beta posteriors per item times city for exploration slots; propensity logged.

420
00:25:30.503 --> 00:25:32.957
Serving (ADR-294).

421
00:25:33.237 --> 00:25:39.594
Candidates precomputed nightly for active users; on-request fallback to popular-by-store for new users.

422
00:25:39.874 --> 00:25:40.898
Consequences.

423
00:25:41.178 --> 00:25:47.386
More logging and data plumbing; exploration costs a little short-term conversion; two serving paths.

424
00:25:47.666 --> 00:25:55.154
In return: a feed that keeps learning, new products that get a fair chance, fresh availability, and a latency budget that holds.

